{
  "note": "Shared cases of the member row key and of the door of a member (contract v0.6.0, mob_addressing.row_key). A row is keyed by the door it was read on: the name as that door knows it on the launch mob's door, and <the door's mob id>/<that name> on the door of another hosted mob. A frame's mob_id and identity are the key's two parts. A row names its door in mob_id, the mob its member sits in in member_mob_id and the member's bare name in member_name. An identity a door is given as one string is read so: it splits at its first separator, and its first part names a mob only when that mob is listed under the same door; else the whole string is a name of the door's own mob. Two members of one door can spell one identity (shared_spelling): the two row members tell them apart, and no reading of the identity does. The gateway's rows and the console's rows read this one file.",
